Great idea about the Narnia quest! :) I think that could be a lot of
fun.

I too imagine the portal being in a closet/wardrobe, to take you to a
wintered wood lit by a lamppost near Cair Paravel, but I like the
structure that you have of random dungeon levels being used to descend
into Aslan's How to get to the Stone Table. That's pretty creative --
I like it. :)


As far as the quest artifact, what about one of the gifts that Father
Christmas gave to Peter, Susan and Lucy?

Peter had a lion-shield and sword -- already enough sword artifacts in
the game, and there wasn't much special about the shield to be worthy
of a quest artifact.
Susan received a bow/arrows and a horn -- we've already got the
Longbow of Diana, but an artifact tooled horn could be kindof cool.
Perhaps it could operate as a normal tooled horn when blown, and when
#invoked it could summon a pet centaur, giant, or other Narnia-themed
beast? Without wanting it to be *too* powerful, it could also convey
half phys damage. The advantage of the Horn is that it was the
artifact that was passed down and used by Narnians other than the
Pevinses.
Perhaps the most interesting artifact to me is Lucy's diamond vial of
healing potion -- I'm imagining this being an artifact diamond that
when #invoked is the same as a potion of full healing. It could convey
MR, or perhaps regen when carried as well.

If you wanted to make the patch for multiple people, then Lucy's
crystal vial would work well for the healer, and the Horn could work
well for anyone (including Knight).

Knight would fit well, but I also like the ineptitude of the children
as they grow through their journey. Perhaps use a tourist as a
"Precocious Child"? :)

All told, great idea! :) If you wound up making this, I'd love to get
a binary copy to play. :)

--clint

